      en: "Dharahara Tower, also known as Bhimsen Tower, was a 61.88-meter tall tower in Kathmandu, Nepal, built in 1832 by Prime Minister Bhimsen Thapa. It served as a lookout and military watchtower. The nine-story tower was a city landmark. The 2015 earthquake completely collapsed it; reconstruction started in 2019. The tower was part of Kathmandu's old city and offered a panoramic view. It was built in Mughal architectural style. Entry was open to the public. Reconstruction is expected to be completed by 2023. The tower symbolizes Nepalese identity and resilience.",
